  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented, and the full test suite passes (1915 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). `mypy` reports no issues on `types.py`.\n\n**Behavior:**\n- `a=b` gives `(\"a\", \"b\")`, and `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, because it splits on the first `=`.\n- `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`, so an empty value is allowed.\n- An input with no `=`, an empty key (`=v`), or an empty string fails with `'<input>' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- A 2-item tuple passes through unchanged.\n- `--help` shows `KEY=VALUE` as the placeholder.\n\n**Changes:**\n- The class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- Docs are updated in `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- There is a new 8.6.0 (Unreleased) entry in `CHANGES.md`.\n- Tests are added in `tests/test_types.py` (valid input, invalid input exiting with code 2, `multiple=True`, help placeholder) and `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n\nI didn't commit anything. The `uv run` calls printed a warning that `VIRTUAL_ENV` doesn't match the project's `.venv`, so uv ignored it and created a `.venv` in the repo for the test runs.",
